---
id: org.dxos.scene
name: Scene
version: 0.1.0
---

One data structure for 2D drawings and 3D scenes. The editor, the assistant and the animator all read and write it.
It has three aspects: a Model of reusable objects, a Layout of positioned elements that place them, and a Scene that
views a layout through a camera. `@dxos/scene` holds the schemas, validation, arrangement and the ECHO form;
`@dxos/diagram` holds its text form (the `scene`, `layout` and `model` blocks of `.dx`); `@dxos/react-ui-scene` draws
it; plugin-canvas makes it an animator stage. The design is `agents/superpowers/specs/2026-10-28-scene-model-design.md`.

## Extensions

The following extension dialects are used in this document.
Each extension is defined in the Appendix or resolved via its URI.

| Term       | URI                         |
| ---------- | --------------------------- |
| `type`     | `org.dxos.mdl.type@1.0`     |
| `feat`     | `org.dxos.mdl.feat@1.0`     |
| `decision` | `org.dxos.mdl.decision@1.0` |

## Types

```mdl
type Model
  desc: >
    `Model<O>`: a library of reusable objects of type O, with no positions; `Model2D` and `Model3D` are its ECHO
    objects (typenames `org.dxos.type.scene.model2d` and `.model3d`), keyed by `key` because ECHO reserves `id`.
  fields:
    name?: string
    objects: Record<string, O>
```

```mdl
type Object
  desc: >
    A reusable definition an element places: a kind, a size (2D `size`, 3D `scale`), style and props. A composite
    object's `parts` is a nested Layout, shown fitted to the frame of each element that places it.
  fields:
    id: string
    kind: string
    style?: Style
    props?: Record<string, any>
    parts?: Ref<Layout2D | Layout3D>  # an id in record form
```

```mdl
type Layout
  desc: >
    `Layout<E>`: elements of type E positioned in one coordinate space, placing objects of its model; `Layout2D` and
    `Layout3D` are its ECHO objects (`org.dxos.type.scene.layout2d` and `.layout3d`), keyed as Model is.
  fields:
    name?: string
    model?: Ref<Model2D | Model3D>    # an id in record form
    elements: Record<string, E>
```

```mdl
type Scene
  desc: >
    `Scene<C>`: a layout seen through a camera of type C; several scenes may share one layout. `Scene2D` and `Scene3D`
    are its ECHO objects (`org.dxos.type.scene.scene2d` and `.scene3d`), keyed as Model is.
  fields:
    name?: string
    theme?: string
    layout: Ref<Layout2D | Layout3D>  # an id in record form
    camera: C
```

```mdl
type BaseElement
  desc: >
    Every item in a layout: a shape, a link, a label or a group. An element places a model `object` or names its own
    `kind`; its own fields win over the object's, and style and props merge.
  fields:
    id: string                      # fixed when the element is created
    object?: string                 # the model object it places
    kind?: string                   # its own kind, when it places no object
    order?: string                  # paint order; z is depth
    layer?: string
    hidden?: boolean
    locked?: boolean
    label?: string
    style?: Style
    from?: Binding                  # a link's ends
    to?: Binding
    members?: string[]              # a group's elements
    arrange?: Arrangement           # how a group places its members
    pinned?: boolean                # placed by a person; arranging leaves it
    props?: Record<string, any>     # kind-specific fields
```

```mdl
type Element2D
  desc: BaseElement with 2D geometry, in canvas pixels.
  fields:
    center?: Vec2
    size?: Size2
    rotation?: number
```

```mdl
type Element3D
  desc: BaseElement with 3D geometry, in scene units; `scale` is the element's size.
  fields:
    center?: Vec3
    scale?: Vec3
    rotation?: Vec3                 # Euler degrees
```

```mdl
type Arrangement
  desc: How a group places its members (ring, grid), kept so it can be re-run.
  fields:
    kind: string
    params?: Record<string, any>
```

```mdl
type Style
  desc: Semantic style tokens shared by both dimensions; a theme resolves them to CSS in 2D and materials in 3D.
  fields:
    hue?: string
    tone?: number
    surface?: string                # solid | tint | glass | none
    border?: boolean
    rounded?: boolean
    opacity?: number
```

```mdl
type Camera3D
  desc: Where a 3D view looks from; angles in degrees, yaw 0 from the front, pitch above the horizon.
  fields:
    target: Vec3
    yaw: number
    pitch: number
    distance: number
    fov: number
    projection: string              # perspective | orthographic
```

## Features

```mdl
feat F-1: One model for 2D and 3D

  req F-1.1: A drawing is a Model of objects, Layouts of elements and Scenes over layouts, each one ECHO object whose records live inside it; types are shared only where 2D and 3D share properties.
  req F-1.2: There is one record kind, Element, for shapes and links alike; a link's ends are Bindings to other elements of its layout.
  req F-1.3: Element ids are never positional, and the id `camera` is reserved for the animator's camera target.
  req F-1.4: A composite object's parts are a nested layout with its own units, scaled to fit the frame of the element that places it.
  req F-1.5: A group keeps its members in its layout's coordinates, and stores its arrangement so it can be re-run; a pinned member is not moved.
  req F-1.6: A solid is an operation tree (union, difference, extrude) over operand elements, recomputed when drawn.
```

```mdl
feat F-2: The text form

  req F-2.1: Records print to `.dx` text and parse back to the same records; printing a parsed canonical document returns the same text.
  req F-2.2: Text that gives a group's arrangement but not its members' positions is arranged when parsed.
  req F-2.3: Parsing reports duplicate ids, the reserved id, kinds from the other dimension, unbound links, missing members, missing layouts, models and objects, and cycles through parts.
```

```mdl
feat F-3: Drawing and animation

  req F-3.1: 2D scenes draw through react-ui-canvas, 3D scenes through Babylon, and a 2D scene may also be drawn in 3D on the ground plane.
  req F-3.2: A renderer skips a link whose end is missing and stops at a parts layout already on its path.
  req F-3.3: Each scene type is an animator stage whose targets are the drawn elements of its layout, keyed by their annotated paths; playback never writes the stored layout.
```

## Changelog

```mdl
decision D-1: Share a type between 2D and 3D only where they share properties; embedding one dimension in the other is a separate mechanism, not a reason to share a root type.
  date: 2026-10-28
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-1.1]
```

```mdl
decision D-2: Do not distinguish nodes from links: every item in a scene is one kind of record, as in tldraw.
  date: 2026-10-28
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [Element, F-1.2]
```

```mdl
decision D-3: The record is called Element, the container Scene, and reusable parts Component and Instance.
  date: 2026-10-28
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [Element, Scene2D, Scene3D]
```

```mdl
decision D-4: A scene is stored as records inside one ECHO object.
  date: 2026-10-28
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [Scene2D, Scene3D, F-1.1]
```

```mdl
decision D-5: The records are the source of truth; the DSL is a lossless text form of them.
  date: 2026-10-28
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-2.1]
```

```mdl
decision D-6: A solid is stored as an operation tree over operand elements and recomputed when loaded, not as a baked mesh.
  date: 2026-10-28
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-1.6]
```

```mdl
decision D-7: Both groups and child scenes exist: a group keeps its members in its parent's coordinates, a child scene has its own and is a separate object.
  date: 2026-10-28
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-1.4, F-1.5]
```

```mdl
decision D-8: A 2D scene can be rendered through a 3D projection.
  date: 2026-10-28
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-3.1]
```

```mdl
decision D-9: A link's ends are Bindings (element id and optional anchor); moving an element moves what is bound to it. Fills in [D-2].
  date: 2026-10-28
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-1.2]
  why: With one record kind, a link's geometry must come from what it connects, as tldraw's bindings do.
```

```mdl
decision D-10: Paint order is `order` and `z` is depth; element ids are fixed at creation and never positional. Fills in [D-2].
  date: 2026-10-28
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [Element, F-1.3]
  why: Animator tracks and DSL edits refer to element ids, and a 3D z cannot share a name with paint order.
```

```mdl
decision D-11: Layout intent is stored on groups as an arrangement, alongside the positions it produces; a hand-placed element is pinned. Fills in [D-5].
  date: 2026-10-28
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-1.5, F-2.2]
  why: Storing positions keeps renderers and the animator free of layout; storing intent lets layout be re-run.
```

```mdl
decision D-12: Each scene and each component is its own ECHO object, and a child scene is reached by Ref. Fills in [D-4].
  date: 2026-10-28
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-1.4]
  why: Undo, sharing and an animator shot each bind to one scene.
```

```mdl
decision D-13: A child scene keeps its own units, scaled to 80% of its frame; a link binds only within its own scene. Fills in [D-7].
  date: 2026-10-28
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-1.4]
  why: The same rule canvas portals use, so a nested scene reads the same in 2D and 3D.
```

```mdl
decision D-14: Style tokens are shared and a theme resolves them per renderer; glass in the presentation theme is a rim shell. Fills in [D-1].
  date: 2026-10-28
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [Style, F-3.1]
  why: The tokens have the same meaning in both dimensions; only how they look differs.
```

```mdl
decision D-15: A lifted 2D scene maps canvas (x, y) to (x/100, 0, −y/100), so its top-down view matches the canvas. Fills in [D-8].
  date: 2026-10-28
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-3.1]
  why: Canvas y runs down the screen, which is −z seen from above at yaw 0.
```

```mdl
decision D-16: The plugin still owns a canvas object, which carries its additional metadata, but the editing, rendering and animation mechanism depends only on `Scene`.
  date: 2026-10-29
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [Scene2D, Scene3D]
```

```mdl
decision D-17: One canvas object type serves both dimensions: its root Ref points at a `Scene2D` or a `Scene3D`, and the editor picks the viewport from the root.
  date: 2026-10-29
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [Scene2D, Scene3D]
```

```mdl
decision D-18: 3D move, rotate and scale handles are Babylon's `GizmoManager` gizmos.
  date: 2026-10-29
  by: user:richburdon
```

```mdl
decision D-19: The 3D viewer orbits, zooms and pans with the mouse; inside an animator stage the animation drives the camera.
  date: 2026-10-29
  by: user:richburdon
```

```mdl
decision D-20: Every drawing is a `Drawing`, so one query finds them all and a user can convert one format into another. `Drawing.content` is a Ref to one content type, each owned by its plugin: `Excalidraw`, `TLDraw` or `Canvas`. plugin-canvas's `Canvas` holds its metadata, including named style classes, and `Canvas.content` is a Ref to a `Scene2D` or `Scene3D`.
  date: 2026-10-29
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [Scene2D, Scene3D]
  supersedes: D-17
```

```mdl
decision D-21: plugin-spacetime is deleted within stage 3, once each of its tools has a test in the new editor; its objects are not migrated.
  date: 2026-10-29
  by: user:richburdon
```

```mdl
decision D-22: plugin-canvas switches to `Scene2D` only when every react-ui-canvas mode runs on it: free, lattice, constrained and scored.
  date: 2026-10-29
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [Scene2D]
```

```mdl
decision D-23: The fields every element shares are the type `BaseElement`; `Element2D` and `Element3D` add their geometry to it.
  date: 2026-10-29
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [BaseElement, Element2D, Element3D]
```

```mdl
decision D-24: A 3D element's location is `center`, as a 2D element's is, not `position`.
  date: 2026-10-29
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [Element3D]
```

```mdl
decision D-25: Both dimensions share one generic `Scene<E, C>` type, over the element and camera types; `Scene2D` and `Scene3D` are built from it.
  date: 2026-10-29
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [Scene, Scene2D, Scene3D]
```

```mdl
decision D-26: `Drawing.canvas` is widened rather than replaced: its Ref accepts the existing `Drawing.Canvas`, which tldraw and excalidraw drawings keep unchanged and unmigrated, or plugin-canvas's typed `Canvas`. Only `dxos.org/scene/2` drawings migrate, to a `Canvas` and a `Scene2D`. The `Canvas` and Scene parts of [D-20] stand.
  date: 2026-10-29
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [Scene2D, Scene3D]
  supersedes: D-20
```

```mdl
decision D-27: A drawing separates three aspects: the Model (reusable objects), the Layout (positioned elements, each placing a model object or defining its shape inline) and the Scene (a layout plus a camera). A 3D animation has one model and several scenes with differently placed elements; a 2D drawing's zoom levels are scenes over one layout. plugin-canvas's `Canvas` holds the model, its layouts and its scenes.
  date: 2026-10-29
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [Scene2D, Scene3D]
  supersedes: D-25
```

```mdl
decision D-28: An animator shot stages a Scene; playback samples the timeline and renders the layout with those values applied, and never writes them back, so scenes that share a layout are unaffected.
  date: 2026-10-29
  by: user:richburdon
```

```mdl
decision D-29: A child scene becomes a composite object: an object's `parts` is its own nested layout, which an element placing the object shows fitted to its frame, and which drill-in opens.
  date: 2026-10-29
  by: user:richburdon
```

```mdl
decision D-30: The group arranger type (ring, grid) is renamed from `Layout` to `Arrangement`, and an element's `layout` field to `arrange`, so `Layout` names the positioned-elements aspect of [D-27].
  date: 2026-10-29
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  why: [D-27] gives `Layout` a new meaning, and two types of one name in one package would be read for each other.
  rejected: Naming the new aspect `Arrangement` instead, which the user called layout.
```

```mdl
decision D-31: In text an element names the model object it places where a kind would go, so an object id may not also be a kind; in records an element has `object` or `kind`, and resolving it applies the object's kind, size, style and props, its own fields winning and style and props merging. Fills in [D-27].
  date: 2026-10-29
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [BaseElement, F-2.1]
  why: The object is the element's type, so it reads in the kind's place, and an element that sets nothing looks exactly like its object.
  rejected: A separate `object=` attribute, which `object` cannot be since it is a keyword of the DSL; a new statement for placing objects.
```

```mdl
decision D-32: In ECHO a Scene holds a Ref to its Layout, a Layout to its Model, and a composite object to its parts Layout; a document is stored layouts first, then models, then each layout's model Ref, then scenes. Fills in [D-27] and [D-29].
  date: 2026-10-29
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [Model, Layout, Scene]
  why: A model's parts usually lead back to layouts that use the model, so the Refs form cycles that only setting a Ref after both objects exist can make.
```

```mdl
decision D-33: A document's text and record form lists scenes, then layouts, then models, with ids unique per kind; the first scene is the root. Fills in [D-27].
  date: 2026-10-29
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-2.1]
  why: A reader meets what is shown before what it is made of; scenes and layouts often share a name, which separate namespaces allow.
```

```mdl
decision D-34: A layout carries renderer-specific `props`, as an element does; a canvas View written as a layout keeps every field the scene model has no slot for under `props.canvas`, so it reads back unchanged. A canvas portal or instance becomes an element placing a composite object (`view:<scene>`, `instance:<composite>`) whose parts is the inner View. Fills in [D-29].
  date: 2026-10-29
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [Layout2D]
  why: The canvas has more node types and fields than the scene model names; keeping the rest lets a canvas move onto layouts without losing any of it.
```

```mdl
decision D-35: The 2D kinds include every built-in canvas node type (cloud, polyline, generator, diagram), so a layout written from a canvas validates. Fills in [D-34].
  date: 2026-10-29
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  why: Validation would otherwise report every migrated cloud or polyline as a kind a 2D scene cannot hold.
```

```mdl
decision D-36: plugin-canvas's `Canvas` keeps the drawing's settings and named style classes; the drawing's content lives in the model, layouts and scenes it lists, and the first scene is the one the drawing opens at. Fills in [D-26] and [D-27].
  date: 2026-10-29
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  why: Settings and style classes belong to the drawing as a whole, not to one layout; everything else has a scene type already.
```

```mdl
decision D-37: A scene canvas migrates as one Layout2D and one Scene2D per View, the root View's first, with the objects its portals and instances place in one Model2D; each scene's camera centres on what its layout holds at zoom 1, since v2 content stored no viewport. The legacy canvas is kept, unreferenced. Fills in [D-36].
  date: 2026-10-29
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  why: A View is both an arrangement and a place a portal opens, so it needs a layout and a scene; keeping the legacy canvas loses nothing if a migration has to be redone.
  rejected: Removing the legacy canvas once migrated.
```

```mdl
decision D-38: An element's `props` keys belong to their writers: the canvas keeps its own fields under `props.canvas` and the illustrator's DSL identity under `props.dsl`, and a write by one keeps the others' keys. Fills in [D-34].
  date: 2026-10-29
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  why: The canvas editor and the illustrator's commands both write the same elements; neither may drop what the other keeps.
```

```mdl
decision D-39: A projection's own model (the constrained projection's constraints, the dynamic projection's graph and overlay) lives in its layout's props, so it persists with the arrangement it constrains and undo patches it; a canvas's settings name the mode it opens in. Fills in [D-34].
  date: 2026-10-29
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  why: Every react-ui-canvas mode must run on Layout2D before the switch (D-22), and those modes are their models.
```

```mdl
decision D-40: A migrated or converted canvas records what it was created from with a `CreatedFrom` relation; a peer that migrated in parallel adopts the winning canvas and replays its edits into it.
  date: 2026-10-29
  by: user:richburdon
```

```mdl
decision D-41: `CreatedFrom` is a generic relation in `@dxos/types` (`org.dxos.relation.createdFrom`), beside `HasSubject` and `AnchoredTo`, with a free `reason` string and a `createdAt` date. Fills in [D-40].
  date: 2026-10-29
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  why: Provenance is not specific to canvases, and `@dxos/types` is where relations every plugin may use already live; plugin-canvas and plugin-illustrator register it in their schema lists.
  rejected: A relation inside plugin-canvas, which plugin-illustrator's conversions could not use without depending on it.
```

```mdl
decision D-42: The winner is the canvas the drawing references. Each other canvas created from the same legacy canvas has every element, layout name, camera and setting field it changed from the legacy content replayed into the winner where the winner still holds the legacy value; where both changed a field, the winner's value stands. Elements only the loser added are added; elements the winner deleted stay deleted; layouts only the loser made are not replayed. The loser is then removed with its scenes, layouts, model and relation. Fills in [D-40].
  date: 2026-10-29
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  why: Both copies came from the same records, so element ids match and the legacy content is a common base for a three-way, field-level merge.
  rejected: Copying the loser's elements wholesale, which would undo the winner's edits.
```

```mdl
decision D-43: A conversion records `CreatedFrom` only when it makes a copy; a conversion that replaces its source removes the source, so there is nothing left to point at.
  date: 2026-10-29
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  why: A relation to a removed object dangles.
```

```mdl
decision D-44: Reconciling a parallel migration also adopts what only the losing canvas made: its layouts and scenes whose keys neither the legacy content nor the winner has move onto the winner, with the model objects the winner lacks (the loser's whole model when the winner has none), so a View a peer made during the race is kept. Otherwise as [D-42].
  date: 2026-10-29
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  supersedes: D-42
  why: Dropping a peer's new View lost user work the replay of edited fields was meant to keep.
  rejected: Copying the loser's layouts, which would break the Refs between a composite object's parts and its model.
```
